WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.076 --> 00:00:20.481
The children quickly realized that the strange man at the door was Eliza's fiancé.

2
00:00:21.341 --> 00:00:24.642
And that an invisible Eliza was holding his hand tightly.

3
00:00:24.662 --> 00:00:29.603
"He keeps saying he can't see me," said Eliza's voice.

4
00:00:29.623 --> 00:00:33.692
"Well, I can't," protested her fiancé.

5
00:00:33.712 --> 00:00:39.074
"I know you have the ring," Gerald whispered to Eliza.

6
00:00:39.094 --> 00:00:40.654
"Go inside."

7
00:00:44.595 --> 00:00:45.135
going on?"

8
00:00:45.616 --> 00:00:48.616
asked the man, who seemed to relax once Eliza released him.

9
00:00:48.636 --> 00:00:50.757
"Have I been acting strange?"

10
00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:55.678
"Very strange," said Mabel.

11
00:00:55.698 --> 00:00:59.339
"You should go home and lie down," said Gerald.

12
00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.800
"The sun is very hot today."

13
00:01:03.016 --> 00:01:06.998
"Yes yes the man said with a puzzled look.

14
00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:08.719
"I'll do that."

15
00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.362
Once he was gone, the children went inside to talk to Eliza.

16
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:18.064
It took a while to convince her that she really was invisible.

17
00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:22.306
She said she'd found the ring in the bed and "borrowed" it.

18
00:01:22.327 --> 00:01:25.308
"Do I have to stay like this?"

19
00:01:25.788 --> 00:01:26.349
she wailed.

20
00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:29.390
"No man will marry a girl he can't see."

21
00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:33.788
"It doesn't last forever," said Mabel kindly.

22
00:01:33.808 --> 00:01:37.669
"And we'll help you," added Kathleen.

23
00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:41.791
"Now let's get Mademoiselle's tea ready," said Gerald.

24
00:01:41.811 --> 00:01:44.191
"And ours!"

25
00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:45.392
said Jimmy.

26
00:01:45.412 --> 00:01:48.632
"No." Gerald looked thoughtful.

27
00:01:48.652 --> 00:01:51.633
"We'll have a picnic and take Eliza.

28
00:01:52.013 --> 00:01:53.094
I'll go get some cakes."

29
00:01:57.855 --> 00:02:01.736
While Gerald was out, Mademoiselle came home from visiting the castle.

30
00:02:03.304 --> 00:02:05.225
She seemed tired and a little sad.

31
00:02:06.927 --> 00:02:11.009
As soon as Gerald returned, the children and Eliza started for the castle.

32
00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.693
They watched the sun go down as they had their picnic on the castle grounds.

33
00:02:15.713 --> 00:02:18.995
"I should go home now," said Mabel.

34
00:02:19.015 --> 00:02:23.818
"Well, I can't go home like this," said Eliza.

35
00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:27.221
She pointed to a white marble temple.

36
00:02:27.241 --> 00:02:31.564
"I'd live in that little white house over there if it had any walls."

37
00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.402
"Oh, you mean the Temple of Apollo," said Mabel.

38
00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.524
"What a lot of steps to clean!"

39
00:02:40.024 --> 00:02:40.764
said Eliza.

40
00:02:40.785 --> 00:02:44.887
"Why do they make houses without walls?

41
00:02:45.447 --> 00:02:47.348
Who'd live in She paused.

42
00:02:48.949 --> 00:02:49.649
"What's that?"

43
00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:54.032
"What?" asked Kathleen and Jimmy together.

44
00:02:54.752 --> 00:02:55.933
They couldn't see anything.

45
00:02:55.953 --> 00:03:00.195
"That white thing coming down the steps," said Eliza.

46
00:03:02.988 --> 00:03:04.769
"Oh! It's a young man.

47
00:03:05.449 --> 00:03:07.330
But he looks like a statue."

48
00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:11.433
"I thought I saw the statues come alive last night!"

49
00:03:12.393 --> 00:03:13.414
exclaimed Gerald.

50
00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:16.175
"I think it happens after sunset."

51
00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:19.897
"I never saw them come alive," said Mabel.

52
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:22.699
"And I've often been in the gardens at night."

53
00:03:22.719 --> 00:03:26.941
"I know I saw them moving," said Gerald.

54
00:03:26.961 --> 00:03:30.743
"I believe you," said Mabel.

55
00:03:30.763 --> 00:03:35.790
"I wonder if you can only see them move when you're invisible."

56
00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.793
"You're probably right," Gerald replied.

57
00:03:39.813 --> 00:03:41.434
"Oh look!"

58
00:03:41.914 --> 00:03:42.655
said Eliza.

59
00:03:42.675 --> 00:03:44.857
"There's another statue!

60
00:03:46.118 --> 00:03:48.079
He's got little wings on his feet!"

61
00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:53.643
"That's probably Hermes, the messenger of the gods," said Gerald.

62
00:03:53.663 --> 00:03:56.245
"What are you talking about?"

63
00:03:56.665 --> 00:03:57.286
asked Jimmy.

64
00:03:57.306 --> 00:03:59.988
"I don't see any moving statues."

65
00:04:01.332 --> 00:04:03.574
The gardens stretched in front of the children.

66
00:04:04.555 --> 00:04:06.756
They could only see the statues standing still.

67
00:04:07.697 --> 00:04:11.759
But Eliza could see statues walking over the lawn and swimming in the lake.

68
00:04:11.779 --> 00:04:16.603
"Oh, here's a dear little boy," she said.

69
00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:21.066
"He's coming right toward me."

70
00:04:22.507 --> 00:04:24.328
The next moment she was screaming.

71
00:04:28.251 --> 00:04:31.777
There was the sound of boots on gravel—Eliza was running away!

72
00:04:31.797 --> 00:04:34.578
"She must have touched the statue!"

73
00:04:35.018 --> 00:04:35.779
cried Gerald.

74
00:04:35.799 --> 00:04:40.241
"Then she became afraid, just like I did last night.

75
00:04:42.042 --> 00:04:43.482
Come on," he added.

76
00:04:43.502 --> 00:04:49.425
"We have to catch her before she frightens everybody in town with her screams."

77
00:04:50.506 --> 00:04:54.147
Mabel stayed at the castle, but the others ran as fast as they could.

78
00:04:56.512 --> 00:04:59.955
They didn't catch up with Eliza until they reached their own back door.

79
00:05:00.275 --> 00:05:04.778
Just as the church clock struck the half-hour, Eliza suddenly reappeared.

80
00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.361
She held out her hand.

81
00:05:10.322 --> 00:05:12.324
The magic ring was on her finger.
